APIs referenced without translating code
----------------------------------------

  Some "// port:" markers name a library API whose documented behaviour the Rust code reproduces
  without translating its source: java.lang.Object/Enum/String/Throwable methods, java.util.logging,
  Guava's ImmutableMap/ImmutableSet builders and multimaps elsewhere, Truth subjects, JUnit's
  TemporaryFolder and Guava testlib's EqualsTester. They add no notice; the report of
  scripts/license_headers.py lists each one.

Binary distributions
--------------------

  The closure-rs executable also contains Rust crates from crates.io (Cargo.lock) and the Rust
  standard library, each under its own license (MIT, Apache-2.0, Unlicense, Zlib), which the
  binary distribution reproduces with the files above: LICENSES/THIRD_PARTY_RUST.md (also in
  the npm package) lists every linked crate with its version,
  license and full license texts, including zlib's for the copy libz-sys builds from source when
  no system zlib is used, and the MIT notice of Microsoft's mimalloc allocator, whose C sources
  libmimalloc-sys compiles into the binary. scripts/third_party_licenses.py writes it from
  Cargo.lock.

  The linux-x64 executable is statically linked (Rust target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl) and also
  contains the C runtime that the Rust toolchain ships for that target:
    musl 1.2.5 (the C library libc.a and the startup objects rcrt1.o, crti.o, crtn.o):
      Copyright (c) 2005-2020 Rich Felker, et al. Licensed under the MIT License; musl's COPYRIGHT
      file, which also names its contributors and the code under other permissive terms, is
      reproduced in LICENSES/MIT-musl.txt.
    LLVM libunwind (libunwind.a) and LLVM compiler-rt (crtbeginS.o, crtendS.o), LLVM 22.1.2:
      Part of the LLVM Project, under the Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions
      (LICENSES/Apache-2.0-WITH-LLVM-exception-libunwind.txt and
      LICENSES/Apache-2.0-WITH-LLVM-exception-compiler-rt.txt).
  LICENSES/THIRD_PARTY_RUST.md lists them with the crates and reproduces both texts.
